      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T16:27:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. I generally feel that if you pass null to a method which is documented to require @NonNull, and you get a NullPointerException, you should be able to figure out that it\u0027s your fault.\n\nBut the API guidelines do suggest using the version with the method, and there is some usage in the existing APIs. So I guess.",
